          "line_end": 41
        }
      ],
      "severity": "moderate",
      "affects_owed_component": false,
      "observation": "Clause 4 of thm:p02-w02-p02-038-empty-comparison says it uses no choice because it fixes one injection of the at most countable symbol set into N, and the annex proof (551-553) says the symbol set is at most countable, citing def:p02-many-sorted-signature. That definition now lets Sort, F and R have any cardinality (variants.tex 35-36), so the cited premise is gone. With countably many sorts, where the variable-form empty-sort variant still applies, and uncountably many function symbols, no such injection exists. The choice-free least-code choice of t_s then fails as written. This is left over from the earlier at-most-countable restriction. It sits in the empty-sort comparison, outside the owed strict reduction and its correspondence."
    },
    {
      "id": "DO-2",
      "path": "handbook/parts/p02/variants.tex",
      "line_start": 180,
      "line_end": 198,
      "related": [
        {
          "path": "handbook/parts/p02/variants.tex",
          "line_start": 36,
          "line_end": 44
        },
        {
          "path": "handbook/parts/p02/many-sorted-and-alternative-first-order-w02b-p02-033.tex",
          "line_start": 407,
          "line_end": 425
        }
      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "affects_owed_component": false,
      "observation": "thm:p02-many-sorted-translation is stated for any strict many-sorted signature, but tr_MS and VarGuard_MS assume the fixed injection of the sorted variables into the countable Var. By thm:p02-w02b-p02-033-no-renaming that injection does not exist when Sort is uncountable. The restriction is announced in the prose of def:p02-many-sorted-signature (36-44), in the w02-p02-038 body (41-52) and in the w02b warning (476-495), and thm:p02-w02b-p02-033-reduction gives the reduction for every strict signature. The problem is presentational: the theorem statement does not carry its own hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "id": "DO-3",
      "path": "handbook/annex/p02/higher-order-supplement.tex",
      "line_start": 22,
      "line_end": 60,
      "severity": "minor",
      "affects_owed_component": false,
      "observation": "The proof that proved=annex:p2.hol.5 attaches to thm:p02-many-sorted-translation is a summary ('Induction on terms, then on well-sorted formulas, gives ...'; 'The same induction gives truth preservation'), and on its own it would count only as partial. GOAL-03 is covered by the complete proofs of thm:p02-w02-p02-038-strict-correspondence (annex w02-p02-038 107-395) and of thm:p02-w02b-p02-033-reduction and thm:p02-w02b-p02-033-variable-form (annex w02b 122-508). The theorem's proved= key does not point to those proofs. The link is made only in prose (w02-p02-038 body 445-447)."
    },
    {
      "id": "DO-4",
      "path": "handbook/parts/p02/variants.tex",
      "line_start": 205,
      "line_end": 209,
      "related": [
        {
          "path": "handbook/parts/p02/variants.tex",
