      "severity": "minor",
      "affects_owed_component": false,
      "observation": "The text asserts that compactness and downward Lowenheim-Skolem transfer, and states when upward enlargement transfers, but gives no argument. Lookup table tab:p02-fol-extensions says compactness is 'Preserved by Theorem thm:p02-many-sorted-translation', and that variable-form theorem is unavailable for uncountably many sorts, where only the parameter form applies. These transfers are not owed by ED26-REQ-D-P3-007-01."
    },
