      ],
      "severity": "minor",
      "affects_owed_component": false,
      "observation": "In def:p02-many-sorted-signature, x^s is schematic for any variable of sort s, as in the formation clause 'sorted quantifiers forall x^s and exists x^s'. These lines (and w02b 51-54) later fix x^s as the designated variable of s. Read literally, the formation clause would then allow quantification only over that one variable. The satisfaction clauses for forall v and exists v with v of any sort (w02-p02-038 145-153) and the w02b example (444-457) fix the intended reading."
